.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-list - List payments for the authenticated wallet (requires login)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns all payments where your wallet is payer or payee.
Requires authentication — run 'rail0 auth login -p 0xKey…' first.

.PP
Filter with --status, --mode, --payer, --payee, --token, --chain-id, --disputed,
--operation, --rail0-id, --reference / --reference-origin, --min-amount / --max-amount, and --created-from /
--created-to (ISO-8601). --operation keeps payments carrying at least one
transaction of that operation — '--operation dispute' finds every payment ever
disputed, which --disputed (an OPEN dispute) does not.

.PP
--status takes several values, repeated or comma-separated, and matches ANY of
them: '--status authorized,partially_captured' is every payment with escrow still
capturable. Each value is checked against the payment-status vocabulary before
any request.

.PP
--min-amount / --max-amount are DECIMALS in token units ('1.00'), like every other
amount flag. Converting them to the base units the gateway filters on needs the
token's decimals, so both --chain-id and --token are required with them — and an
amount range only means something within one token anyway.

.PP
\&'--scope all' is the operator's list: every payment on the gateway, with the same
filters, and it needs an admin session (403 otherwise — never silently narrowed to
your own). Three filters exist only there and are refused without it: --account
(payments whose payee is one of that account's wallets), --has-error (payments
carrying a last_error_code, or --has-error=false for the clean ones) and
--expiring-within (authorized payments whose hold lapses within that duration,
\&'24h' or '90m', up to 90 days).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	With --scope all: payments whose payee is one of this account's wallets

.PP
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	Fetch every page (ignores --page)

.PP
\fB--chain-id\fP=0
	Filter by EVM chain ID

.PP
\fB--created-from\fP=""
	Only payments created at/after this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--created-to\fP=""
	Only payments created at/before this ISO-8601 time

.PP
\fB--disputed\fP[=false]
	Filter by whether an open dispute exists

.PP
\fB--expiring-within\fP=0s
	With --scope all: authorized payments whose hold lapses within this duration (e.g. 24h; max 90 days)

.PP
\fB--has-error\fP[=false]
	With --scope all: payments carrying a last_error_code (--has-error=false: none)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--max-amount\fP=""
	Maximum amount as a decimal in token units (inclusive); needs --chain-id and --token

.PP
\fB--min-amount\fP=""
	Minimum amount as a decimal in token units (inclusive); needs --chain-id and --token

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Filter by mode (authorize or charge)

.PP
\fB--operation\fP=""
	Only payments with at least one transaction of this operation (e.g. dispute, refund)

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--payee\fP=""
	Filter by payee address

.PP
\fB--payer\fP=""
	Filter by payer address

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--rail0-id\fP=""
	Filter by the logical on-chain payment id (0x…)

.PP
\fB--reference\fP=""
	Filter by the payment's identifier in the merchant's own system (exact)

.PP
\fB--reference-origin\fP=""
	Filter by the system the reference comes from

.PP
\fB--scope\fP=""
	mine (default): your wallet's payments; all: every payment on the gateway (admin only)

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields (e.g. -created_at,amount)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=[]
	Filter by payment status; repeat or comma-separate for any of several (e.g. authorized,partially_captured)

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	Filter by token address


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments list
  rail0 payments list --sort -created_at
  rail0 payments list --status authorized --mode charge
  rail0 payments list --status authorized,partially_captured
  rail0 payments list --chain-id 5042002 --disputed
  rail0 payments list --chain-id 5042002 --token 0x3600… --min-amount 1.00 --created-from 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
  rail0 payments list --scope all --has-error                # admin: every payment with an error, any account
  rail0 payments list --scope all --expiring-within 24h      # admin: holds lapsing within a day
  rail0 payments list --scope all --account 019e748b-…       # admin: one merchant's incoming payments
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
